---
const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).href;
const publishYear = 2026;
const year = parseInt(
  new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
    timeZone: "America/Chicago",
    year: "numeric",
  }),
);
const copyright =
  year > publishYear
    ? `© ${publishYear}-${year} Matthew Mehrtens`
    : `© ${publishYear} Matthew Mehrtens`;
---

<html lang="en-US">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>Matthew Mehrtens</title>
    <meta name="author" content="Matthew Mehrtens" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Personal site of Matthew Mehrtens—a Ph.D. student in engineering mechanics at Iowa State University with a deep passion for computers and consumer technology."
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <a href="#main">Skip to main</a>

    <header>
      <a href="/">Matthew Mehrtens</a>
      <nav aria-label="primary">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/" aria-current="page">About Me</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog">Blog</a></li>
          <li><a href="/projects">Projects</a></li>
          <li><a href="/contact">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
      <h1>About Me</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a Ph.D. student at Iowa State University (<abbr>ISU</abbr>) studying
        <a
          href="https://www.grad-college.iastate.edu/programs/engineering_mechanics"
          >engineering mechanics</a
        >, with a focus on <a
          href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Continuum_mechanics"
          >solid continuum mechanics</a
        > and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fluid_dynamics"
          >fluid dynamics</a
        >. My research is on the topological optimization of
        <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solid-propellant_rocket"
          >solid composite propellants (<abbr>SCP</abbr>)</a
        >, work supported by the <a
          href="https://ndseg.sysplus.com/NDSEG/about/"
          >National Defense Science and Engineering Graduate (<abbr>NDSEG</abbr
          >) Fellowship</a
        > awarded to me in spring 2026. I received my B.S. in aerospace engineering
        from Iowa State in May 2025, during which I spent two and a half years as
        a systems and software engineering intern at <a
          href="https://www.rtx.com/collinsaerospace">Collins Aerospace</a
        >. I'm currently a fellow in the
        <a
          href="https://www.lanl.gov/engage/organizations/xcp/computational-physics-student-summer-workshop"
          >2026 Computational Physics Student Summer Workshop</a
        > at <a href="https://www.lanl.gov"
          >Los Alamos National Laboratory (<abbr>LANL</abbr>)</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        Although my education and experience is deeply intertwined with
        aerospace and national defense, my passion is for computers and consumer
        technology. I'm deeply fascinated by topics such as compilers,
        networking, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_of_things"
          >Internet of Things (<abbr>IoT</abbr>)</a
        >, and programming language design. I'm drawn to consumer technology
        because of the fundamental constraints associated with the design and
        engineering of consumer products—and by the (perhaps naïve) aspiration
        that improving a product—even marginally—has the potential to directly
        improve the lives of thousands, millions, or even billions of people,
        depending on the size of the market.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of tech and programming, I find my happy place listening to <a
          href="https://music.apple.com/profile/mcmehrtens"
          rel="me">music</a
        >, watching movies, listening to podcasts, drinking coffee, and spending
        quality time with my close friends. My goals in life are to leave a
        positive, lasting impact on the world, either through my interactions
        with the people I meet or the work I do in my career, and to learn
        everything there is about computers and technology writ large.
      </p>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p><small>{copyright}</small></p>
      <nav aria-label="legal">
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/mcmehrtens/mehrtens.com">Source</a>
          </li>
          <li><a href="/privacy" rel="privacy-policy">Privacy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/terms" rel="terms-of-service">Terms</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
